<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahi Bajaj Sagar Dam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahi Bajaj Sagar Dam is a large dam on the Mahi river near Banswara in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in the 1970s and 1980s for irrigation and hydroelectric power. Named after the independence activist Jamnalal Bajaj, it created a reservoir dotted with islands, and its canals irrigate much of the largely tribal Banswara district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahi-bajaj-sagar-dam.jpg" alt="Mahi Bajaj Sagar Dam" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ibrahim Bohra · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahi_Bajaj_Sagar_Dam,_Banswara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
